  "result": "The backend for workspace slug renames is in place, following ADR 0005 where it disagrees with the product notes. The full suite passes (631 tests), with typecheck and lint clean.\n\n- **No existing test needed changing:** none of the visible tests encoded behaviour this alters. I added `tests/services/organization-service.rename.test.ts` to cover the ADR rules.\n- **`updatedAt` is not bumped on rename:** I read \"nothing else about the workspace changes\" literally, so only the slug column is written. Other organization writes do bump it; say if you want the rename to as well.\n- **`updateOrg` no longer writes a slug:** the repository patch used to accept one and store it as given, which would have bypassed the rename rules.\n- **Audit row is written directly by the service:** there is no bus listener for it, so it is recorded exactly once whether or not the audit listeners are attached.\n- **New table:** retired slugs live in `organization_retired_slugs`, created by `migrate.ts` and cleared by the seed.",
